<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.disk.logs ~ the shore's own log: counts by kind, then each record

`log` reads the vessel's log as records, one per distinct event: the counts by kind first, then each record. `kind=` names one kind, `held=true` the unacknowledged, and `boot=<id>` one boot's ring. With no vessel answering, the verb reads the flat `run/vessel-live.log` and its ash. It writes nothing and asks no hand.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ the-log · the-held · one-kind

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`the-log` params=`~ the counts by kind, then each record`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`the-held` params=`held/true ~ the records no person acknowledged`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`one-kind` params=`kind/standoff ~ the records of one kind`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ kind · held · boot

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`kind` params=`takes/kind ~ one kind of record`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`held` params=`kind/switch ~ the unacknowledged records`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`boot` params=`takes/boot-id ~ one boot's ring`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ read

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`read` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ a read of the vessel's log; with no vessel, the flat run/vessel-live.log`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

